    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 in `AcceptanceTest` (which is the full suite here), including the two new postcode tests plus the backward-compat \"without postcode\" case.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional 4-digit `postcode` to owners, validated against the city's region when present, and stored/returned when given \u2014 keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (`^[0-9]{4}$`, not in `required`). This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` with `getPostcode`/`setPostcode`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `postcode` field with `@Column(name = \"postcode\")` and accessors.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added a `postcode` column so it persists.\n\n4. **`OwnerPostcode.java`** (new helper, mirroring `OwnerAddress`/`OwnerTelephone`) \u2014 the validation logic: null/blank is accepted (optional); a present value must be 4 digits; when the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) the postcode must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); an unknown-region city accepts any 4-digit postcode.\n\n5. **`OwnerPostcodeInvalidException` + handler + escalation YAML** \u2014 following the existing checked-exception \u2192 400 pattern (`{\"errors\":[\"postcode\"]}`).\n\n6. **Wiring** \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields` (POST create path) calls `OwnerPostcode.validate(...)` after the required-field checks; `ApplyOwner` (PUT update path) validates and copies `postcode` too, so updates behave consistently. The mapper maps `postcode` automatically by name.\n\nPostcode validation runs only when a value is present, so an owner created without one is still accepted.",
